Derived data, listed separately because its provenance is not a licence
question that has been settled here:

data/chipdb/ and src/python/cli/chipdb.py are produced by
scripts/gen_chipdb.py from the source of the Linux kernel, which is GPL-2.0
only. The extracted content is identifiers, bit masks and part names — facts
about hardware, most of which also appear in vendor datasheets — but the
selection is the kernel's. The generated files record the kernel version and
commit they came from. Anyone redistributing this firmware commercially
should form their own view, or take advice, rather than rely on this note.
